<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maximilian I Joseph of Bavaria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1756">1756</a>–<a href="/years/1825">1825</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Maximilian IV Joseph</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maximilian I Joseph was the first King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>. Elector of Bavaria as Maximilian IV Joseph from 1799, he allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>, gained <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franconia">Franconia</a>, Swabian lands and imperial cities, and was proclaimed king on 1 January 1806. With his minister Montgelas he modernised the administration, and he changed sides in 1813 in time to keep most of his gains. In 1818 he granted Bavaria a constitution. He died in 1825.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maximilian-i-joseph-of-bavaria.jpg" alt="Maximilian I Joseph of Bavaria" width="320" height="469" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joseph Karl Stieler · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Max_I_Joseph_in_Coronation_Robe.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
